#15235
Throne Room Of The Ghouls~
You step into an ornately decorated throne room, home of the King and Queen of
the Ghoul Kingdom.  Decorations and trophies from all over the Realm stand in
places of honor about the room.  Your eye is drawn to two large thrones,
carved of a strange wood, sitting in the back of the room.
~
0 1032 0
D1
This portal leads somewhere mysterious.
~
portal~
8389671 15044 15236
D3
A hallway filled with fun magic and music.
~
~
0 0 15234
E
throne thrones~
The two majestic thrones are not actually carved of wood but, more accurately,
are shaped from 2 tree's, grown for the purpose of seating the most mighty of
the Ghouls.  The larger has the ghoul rune for "D" placed in it, while the
other has the ghoul rune for "E" engraved.
~
S
#15236
The Ghoul Suite~
This special room is for the King and Queen of the Ghouls, and any special
guests they may let enter.  A large ebony dining table sits at one end,
surrounded by plush, comfortable chairs.  An inviting pile of sleeping
pillows, crafted of the finest of magical materials, lies at the other end of
the room.  Fantastic decorations hang from the walls and stand on small
pedestals.  What a great place to either have a party or just relax!
~
0 1048584 0
D3
This portal leads back to the Throne Room.
~
portal~
8389671 15044 15235
E
pillows plush sleeping~
Ghouls being more decadent then other races, sleep in piles of pillows instead
of having dedicated beds.  This allows them to reshape and recreate the
sleeping area as needs and moods see fit.  These particular pillows are indeed
magical, and shift at will to the desires of the King and Queen of the Ghouls.
~
E
table dining chairs~
The large table in the room is crafted of ebony, yet you get the feel of
strong magic emanating from it.  This table has the ability to enlarge, shrink
and create chairs depending on how many are needed at the time.  It was a gift
from the Lord of the Elves to King Drazuk, in return for some help with a
nasty demon.
~
S
#15237
The Dark Library~
You enter a dark room, which obviously belongs to the Master Mage of the
Ghouls.  Many artifacts of extreme power lie about, covered by their own
special spells of protection.  You get the feeling you don't belong in this
room at all.
~
